<title>BELGIUM: Belgian supermarket workers threaten Easter strike.</title>
<headline>Belgian supermarket workers threaten Easter strike.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers in the Belgian food retail industry on Friday threatened a strike over the Easter weekend if employers refused to meet demands for improved job conditions.</p>
<p>&quot;Negotiations with employers in the supermarkets and food sectors have reached total deadlock,&quot; the SETCa trade union said in a statement. &quot;The union organisations have today delivered a strike warning which runs out on the eve of the Easter Weekend.&quot;</p>
<p>Union demands include job security, improved contracts for part-time workers and shorter working time.</p>
<p>Among the retailers involved were GIB group's GB supermarkets and Biggs hypermarkets, Delhaize and CORA.</p>
